Build with a C library without getc_unlocked() and with newer clang.

zedBSD's C library has flockfile() and funlockfile() but not
getc_unlocked().  pango_read_line() takes the stream's lock with
flockfile() and reads with getc_unlocked(), which was an implicit
declaration there.  Meson now checks for the function and records
HAVE_GETC_UNLOCKED; without it the read is getc(), as on Windows, which
takes the same, already held, recursive lock.

Pango builds with -Werror=unused-but-set-variable.  The clang of the zedBSD
toolchain (LLVM 23) puts -Wunused-but-set-global in that group and reports
the parent_class variable that G_DEFINE_TYPE defines in files that do not
chain up, so pango-fontset.c and others stopped.  That one diagnostic stays
a warning, as it is in GLib's own build.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -50,6 +50,12 @@
 pango_osxversion = [osx_current, '@0@.@1@.0'.format(osx_current, pango_interface_age)]
 
 cc = meson.get_compiler('c')
+
+# A C library may lack getc_unlocked() (zedBSD); pango-utils.c then reads
+# with getc() inside the flockfile() it already holds.
+if cc.has_function('getc_unlocked', prefix: '#include <stdio.h>')
+  pango_conf.set('HAVE_GETC_UNLOCKED', 1)
+endif
 cpp = meson.get_compiler('cpp')
 host_system = host_machine.system()
 
@@ -145,6 +151,9 @@
     '-Werror=empty-body',
     '-Werror=write-strings',
     '-Werror=unused-but-set-variable',
+    # Newer clang counts an unused G_DEFINE_TYPE parent_class, a file-scope
+    # variable, in the group above; it stays a warning, as elsewhere.
+    '-Wno-error=unused-but-set-global',
     '-Wundef', # FIXME: https://bugzilla.gnome.org/show_bug.cgi?id=792481
   ]
 
--- a/pango/pango-utils.c
+++ b/pango/pango-utils.c
@@ -47,6 +47,12 @@
 
 #endif
 
+#if !defined(G_OS_WIN32) && !defined(HAVE_GETC_UNLOCKED)
+/* Without getc_unlocked() (zedBSD), getc() is the same read; the caller
+ * holds the stream's lock through flockfile() either way. */
+#define getc_unlocked(f) getc(f)
+#endif
+
 /**
  * pango_version:
  *
